BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194582@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260713T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T210000
SUMMARY:Boston’s Exclusive First-Look Screening of "The Odyssey"
LOCATION:Offsite: AMC Boston Common
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 20 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1945
 82\n\n6:30PM Doors Open\, 7:00PM-10:00PM Screening\nBe among the first to 
 experience one of the year's most anticipated cinematic events with a firs
 t look screening of Christopher Nolan's highly anticipated adaptation of T
 he Odyssey.\n\nThis summer\, defy the gods. Universal Pictures proudly pre
 sents the new film by Christopher Nolan. A sweeping mythological epic insp
 ired by Homer's timeless poem\, The Odyssey\, staring Matt Damon\, Tom H
 olland\, Anne Hathaway\, Robert Pattison\, Lupita Nyong'o\, Zendaya and\, 
 Charlize Theron. The film follows Odysseus\, the legendary King of Ithaca 
 perilous decade- long journey home after the Trojan War as he confronts my
 thical creatures\, vengeful gods\, and extraordinary trials in a relentles
 s quest to reunite with his wife\, Penelope.\n\nJoin us for an unforgettab
 le evening of epic storytelling\, breathtaking spectacle\, and one of the 
 year's most anticipated cinematic experiences.\n\n*This event is complimen
 tary and reserved for members only. Please note that the screening will be
 gin promptly at 7:00PM with no trailers preceding the film.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194582
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191168@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260714T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T190000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Man Made" with Karen Korellis Reuther
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimit
 ed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191168\n\n5:00PM Re
 ception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if the world around us was not designed 
 with everyone in mind?\n\nJoin us for an illuminating conversation with Ka
 ren Korellis Reuther - designer\, educator\, inclusion advocate\, and auth
 or for an exclusive first look of the forthcoming book MAN-MADE: How We D
 esigned a World That Leaves Women Out\, and How We Can Make It Right. Draw
 ing on more than four decades of experience\, including leadership roles a
 t Nike and Reebok and her current work at Harvard's Graduate School of Des
 ign\, Karen explores the hidden ways gender bias has been built into the p
 roducts\, systems\, and spaces we encounter every day.\n\nFrom personal pr
 otective equipment and athletic footwear to healthcare\, transportation\, 
 and public infrastructure\, MAN-MADE reveals how design decisions rooted
  in a male default continue to shape women's experiences\, often with prof
 ound consequences. Through compelling research\, real-world examples\, and
  a forward-looking vision for change\, Karen invites us to reconsider the 
 world we have inherited - and imagine one designed for everyone.\n\n*This 
 event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refr
 eshments will be served. A pre-release of the book will be available for p
 urchase at this event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191168
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-194581@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260715T133000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T150000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Gallery by Denise Matejic 
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 35 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1945
 81\n\n1:30PM Reception\, 2:00PM Discussion\nPlease join The 'Quin House ar
 t curator\, Kate Chertavian for a discussion together with The ‘Quin Hou
 se Co-Founder Sandy Edgerley on the works of her mother\, artist Denise Ma
 tejic. On view in the Terrace through July 23rd\, the pop-up exhibition fe
 atures 21 artworks in a variety of media created throughout her career. In
 spired by the rural landscapes and cityscapes of Western Europe where she 
 grew up\, as well as the suburban landscape here in New England and beyond
 \, her work is a celebration of the beauty found in the world around us. T
 ogether\, Kate and Sandy will explore Denise's artistic practice and how i
 t has inspired Sandy's lifelong love of art. Members will enjoy this after
 noon experience over tea and light bites.  \n\n*This event is compliment
 ary and reserved for members only.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/194581
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191172@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260715T200000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T223000
SUMMARY:Sail Boston: Luxury Yacht Valiant
LOCATION:Offsite: Rowes Wharf Gate C
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Waitlis
 t Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191172\n\nAs Bo
 ston welcomes a once-in-a-generation gathering of the world's most magnifi
 cent tall ships in celebration of America's 250th anniversary\, join fello
 w members aboard luxury yacht Valiant for an unforgettable evening on the 
 harbor.\n\nDeparting from Rowes Wharf\, this exclusive cruise offers a fro
 nt-row vantage point to Sail Boston 2026\, as an international fleet of hi
 storic tall ships and military vessels fills the harbor in a remarkable di
 splay of maritime tradition and global camaraderie. As dusk settles over t
 he city\, enjoy unparalleled views of the fleet before the evening culmina
 tes with a spectacular fireworks display illuminating the Boston skyline.\
 n\nThroughout the cruise\, guests will enjoy an open bar and a selection o
 f elevated bites while taking in one of the most anticipated events of the
  Semiquincentennial celebration from the best seat in the harbor.\n\n*This
  event is offered at $295 per person and is reserved for members\, plus 
 one registered guest age 21+. Complimentary light bites and refreshments w
 ill be served. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
  Please note that this event will take place rain or shine. Valiant is par
 tially covered\, and in the event of rough water conditions\, the vessel w
 ill remain docked. Members will meet at Rowes Wharf Gate C\, located direc
 tly in front of the Boston Harbor Hotel. Parking is available at the Bost
 on Harbor Hotel.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191172
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191169@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260716T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260716T140000
SUMMARY: Serendipity Lunch - The Creative Exchange
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: $80.00 per person\nAvailability:
  15 spots left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse
 .com/events/191169\n\nContinuing the "Curated Connections" extension of th
 e Serendipity series\, join us for lunch convening members who are involve
 d in—or inspired by—the performing arts. From actors\, musicians\, dan
 cers\, directors\, and producers to passionate patrons and enthusiasts\, t
 his month's commonality will spark engaging conversation through a curated
  deck of prompts facilitated by our Membership team.\n\nCurious? Set again
 st the backdrop of lunch in Lunasol\, members will enjoy meaningful connec
 tions and lively discussion around creativity\, performance\, storytelling
 \, and the cultural impact of the arts. Whether you're center stage or in 
 the audience\, you'll leave with new perspectives\, new connections\, and 
 a deeper appreciation for the vibrant performing arts community within The
  'Quin—all while enjoying a thoughtful lunch prepared by the chef.\n\n*T
 ickets are $80 per person\, plus tax\, and are reserved for members only. 
 Cancellations within 48 hours of the event\, or failure to attend\, will b
 e charged in full. Please inform us of any dietary needs or restrictions b
 y emailing happening@thequin.com at least 72 hours prior to the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191169
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-192823@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260718T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260718T173000
SUMMARY:An Evening with Martini Master Alessandro Palazzi
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You 
 are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192823\n
 \nThere are bartenders\, and then there are bartenders whose names have be
 come synonymous with an institution. Alessandro Palazzi belongs firmly in 
 the latter category. The celebrated Italian mixologist has spent years sha
 ping the cocktail culture of London's legendary Duke's Bar\, where his met
 iculous approach to hospitality and his famously cold martinis have earned
  him a devoted international following.\n\nKnown for his effortless charm\
 , encyclopedic knowledge of spirits\, and flair for storytelling\, Alessan
 dro has elevated the martini from a simple cocktail to a memorable ritual.
  His tableside preparation has become one of London's most sought-after ex
 periences\, drawing discerning travelers\, industry leaders\, and cocktail
  enthusiasts from around the world.\n\nThe 'Quin House is delighted to wel
 come Alessandro for a rare Boston appearance on Saturday\, July 18th and a
 gain\, on Saturday July 25th. Members will have the opportunity to learn f
 irsthand what separates a good cocktail from a truly exceptional one durin
 g an intimate masterclass covering technique\, history\, and the finer poi
 nts of martini-making\, presented in partnership with Procera Gin\, the aw
 ard-winning Nairobi-based spirit crafted with fresh African juniper and ce
 lebrated for redefining luxury gin through exceptional African botanicals 
 and craftsmanship.\n\nFollowing this class\, Alessandro will take over The
  Reading Room for the evening\, where all members can enjoy the comforts o
 f the Reading Room and martinis crafted by one of the hospitality world's 
 most respected figures.\n\n*This event is offered at $100 per member and i
 s reserved for members only. Cancellations made within 48 hours of the eve
 nt\, or failure to attend\, will result in a full charge. Light bites and 
 refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192823
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-189619@thequinhouse.com
